            <ArticleTitle>[Coronary-cavitary fistula after resection of vascularized left atrial myxoma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>487-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 52-year-old man with left atrial myxoma, in whom postoperative angiographic control revealed a coronary-cavitary fistula originated from a previous atrial branch from the circumflex coronary artery. These fistulas should be considered in cases of revascularized atrial myxoma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
